+      "description": "Send typed text as if a speech recognizer had heard it - the simplest way for a program to 'say' a phrase such as 'infantry platoon', with a SendInk stroke or on its own. Use it when a symbol or task is described in words: send the phrase with SendPenDown and SendInk strokes for its place (a point, a line or an area outline), and STP produces the code and properties. For a symbol whose code is already in the user's data, use AddSymbol. Numbers and letters are converted server-side to spoken form (e.g. 'A 3 1' becomes 'alpha three one'); startTime defaults to now and the utterance is taken to last 0.5 s. Fire and forget: the engine sends no reply. SpeechParsed (to the caller) always follows, SpeechRecognized carries the phrase that integrated, and a recognized symbol or task arrives as SymbolAdded / TaskAdded. Text the grammar does not match gives SpeechParsed with no alternates and nothing else; missing text is silently ignored.",
